## Summary

The `Transform.transformMatrix` setter throws for every matrix, because it calls `eulerAngles()` on the plain object that `Matrix4.decompose` returns. `ThreeMfImporter` uses this setter for each build item, so `Scene.open` fails for every 3MF file that has a build item, including one written by `Scene.save` in the same session.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux)
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

const { Transform } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Matrix4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

try { new Transform().transformMatrix = new Matrix4(); } catch (e) { console.log(e.constructor.name + ': ' + e.message); }

const scene = new Scene();
scene.rootNode.createChildNode('n', triangle());
scene.save('t.3mf');
try { new Scene().open('t.3mf'); } catch (e) { console.log(e.constructor.name + ': ' + e.message); }
```

## Expected

The matrix is applied to the transform, and the 3MF file is read back into a scene with one child node.

## Actual result

```
TypeError: rotation[0].eulerAngles is not a function
TypeError: rotation[0].eulerAngles is not a function
```
The existing test `Test3MFRoundTrip > testRoundTripExportImport` fails with the same error.

## Where in the repository

- `src/aspose/threed/Transform.ts:160`: `this._eulerAngles = rotation[0].eulerAngles();`
- `src/aspose/threed/utilities/Matrix4.ts:287`: `decompose` stores `rotation[0] = { w, x, y, z };`, a plain object rather than a `Quaternion`
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/threemf/ThreeMfImporter.ts:289`: `node.transform.transformMatrix = transform;`

