## Summary

`scene.save('x.stl')` writes a file that is not a valid STL. For a triangle with control points (10, 20, 30), (11, 20, 30) and (10, 21, 30), the ASCII output lists the polygon indices `0 1 2` on a single `vertex` line, and the binary output is 50 bytes, a single record without the 80-byte header or the triangle count. Re-opening the ASCII file gives a mesh with control points `[0, 1, 2]` and no polygons.

## Environment

- Revision `66cb26df3b031f0bf6976d4e88dc89721983afa4` (default branch `master`)
- Node.js v22.23.3 and npm 10.9.9 (Docker image `node:22-slim`, Linux)
- `npm install` and `npm run build` complete without errors; verified on 2026-10-16

## Steps to reproduce

```sh
npm install
npm run build
node repro.js   # repro.js holds the script below, saved in the repository root
```

```js
const fs = require('fs');
const { Scene } = require('./dist/aspose/threed');
const { Mesh } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/entities');
const { Vector4 } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/utilities');

function triangle() {
  const mesh = new Mesh('tri');
  mesh.controlPoints = [new Vector4(10, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(11, 20, 30, 1), new Vector4(10, 21, 30, 1)];
  mesh.createPolygon(0, 1, 2);
  return mesh;
}

const { StlSaveOptions } = require('./dist/aspose/threed/formats/stl');

const scene = new Scene();
scene.rootNode.createChildNode('n', triangle());

scene.save('out_ascii.stl');
console.log(fs.readFileSync('out_ascii.stl', 'utf8'));

const options = new StlSaveOptions();
options.binaryMode = true;
scene.save('out_binary.stl', options);
console.log('binary STL size:', fs.statSync('out_binary.stl').size, 'bytes');
```

## Expected

ASCII: one `facet normal` with the computed normal and three lines `vertex 10 20 30`, `vertex 11 20 30`, `vertex 10 21 30`. Binary: 134 bytes (80-byte header, 4-byte triangle count, one 50-byte record with the normal and the three vertices).

## Actual result

```
solid Scene
  facet normal 0 0 0
    outer loop
      vertex 0 1 2
    endloop
  endfacet
endsolid Scene

binary STL size: 50 bytes
```
The existing test `TestSceneSaveSTL > testRoundtripFile` fails for the same reason (`expect(mesh2.polygonCount).toBe(1)` receives `0`).

## Where in the repository

- `src/aspose/threed/formats/stl/StlExporter.ts:82` writes `tri[0] tri[1] tri[2]`, which are polygon indices from `Mesh.polygons`, as the vertex of the facet
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/stl/StlExporter.ts:118-120` writes the same indices as floats into the vertex slots of the binary record
- `src/aspose/threed/formats/stl/StlExporter.ts:104-123` writes the header, the count and each record as separate `stream.write(Buffer)` calls, and `src/aspose/threed/Scene.ts:325` handles each Buffer write for a file path with `fs.writeFileSync(path, data)`, which replaces the file, so only the last record remains
- `tests/test_scene_save_stl.test.ts:77`

